# SMART RETURN. Press SAVE somewhere in the abyss, drive off, flip RETURN: the sub heads straight back to the saved
# spot instead of retracing its path, slows down as it arrives, holds position there, and goes over or under rock its
# wall sensors bump into. Tested in sandbox/world/smart_return.sbx (the Drone Range).
#
# Why it works this way (reference/VEHICLE_MECHANICS.md):
#  * the nav terminal is the only source of position: current_position_x (m) and current_position_y (depth in m,
#    positive down), plus current_velocity_x/y in km/h (y positive = sinking);
#  * no signal can switch on the autopilot or give it a target, so the circuit steers through velocity_in "x,y"
#    (y positive = down), which the terminal applies at once and keeps until the next signal;
#  * there is no rangefinder: rock is seen by motion detectors set to Target=Wall, mounted outside the hull, and they
#    only see rock while the sub is moving;
#  * a sub has a lot of momentum and little drag, so the circuit asks for a SPEED (2.5 m/s at most, less as the spot
#    gets close) and the engine only makes up the difference: it can stop within the 4 m its sensors look ahead.
name smart_return
box nav
note "SMART RETURN: HOW IT WORKS" "SAVE (in5) opens two memories for 0.1 s: they keep the nav position at that moment (they also keep the starting spot until then).\nWanted speed = 0.15 x distance, at most 2.5 m/s across and 1.5 m/s up or down; engine and ballast = 60 x (wanted - actual speed). That stops the sub on the spot instead of overshooting.\nRock: while heading right and the right sensor (in7) sees rock (or left and in8), it is BLOCKED for 3 s: it backs off gently and goes up, or down if the spot is deeper or there's rock above (in9) and none below (in0). It remembers rock above for 6 s, so it doesn't turn back up into an overhang. After a detour it holds its depth for 6 s more while moving across, to get past the rock before heading for the spot again.\nOnly while RETURN (in6) is on does it drive (velocity_in). Switching it off sends 0,0 once, so the sub doesn't keep the last command.\nDisplays: status (MANUAL, RETURN, DETOUR, ARRIVED within 3 m) and distance."
note "WIRING" "in1 <- nav current_position_x, in2 <- nav current_position_y, in3 <- nav current_velocity_x, in4 <- nav current_velocity_y\nin5 <- SAVE button, in6 <- RETURN lever (1 = go back)\nin7 <- wall sensor right, in8 <- wall sensor left, in9 <- wall sensor above, in0 <- wall sensor below (motion detectors, Target=Wall)\nout1 -> nav velocity_in, out2 -> status display, out3 -> distance display\nThe nav terminal's own velocity_x_out -> engine set_force and velocity_y_out -> ballast pumps set_targetlevel stay as in vanilla."
# --- the saved spot
c lk or TimeFrame=0.1
c sx mem Value=0
c sy mem Value=0
w in5 lk.1
w lk.out sx.lock_state sy.lock_state
w in1 sx.in ex.2
w in2 sy.in ey.2
c ex sub
c ey sub
w sx.out ex.1
w sy.out ey.1
# --- speed control: wanted speed from the distance, engine from the speed error
c kp mem Value=0.15
c kms mem Value=0.2778
c tvx mul ClampMin=-2.5 ClampMax=2.5
c tvy mul ClampMin=-1.5 ClampMax=1.5
w ex.out tvx.1
w ey.out tvy.1
w kp.out tvx.2 tvy.2
c vx mul
c vy mul
w in3 vx.1
w in4 vy.1
w kms.out vx.2 vy.2
c evx sub
c evy sub
w tvx.out evx.1
w vx.out evx.2
w tvy.out evy.1
w vy.out evy.2
c kv mem Value=60
c cx mul ClampMin=-100 ClampMax=100
c cy mul ClampMin=-100 ClampMax=100
w evx.out cx.1
w evy.out cy.1
w kv.out cx.2 cy.2
# --- rock ahead: blocked while heading into a side sensor that sees rock, held 3 s
c zero mem Value=0
c gR greater
c gL greater
w cx.out gR.1 gL.2
w zero.out gR.2 gL.1
c bR and
c bL and
w gR.out bR.1
w in7 bR.2
w gL.out bL.1
w in8 bL.2
c blk or TimeFrame=3
w bR.out blk.1
w bL.out blk.2
# across: back off gently while blocked
c kb mem Value=-0.15
c bk mul
w cx.out bk.1
w kb.out bk.2
c xm mux
w blk.out xm.set_input
w cx.out xm.signal_in0
w bk.out xm.signal_in1
# up or down around it: down if the spot is more than 5 m deeper or there was rock above in the last 6 s (so after
# bumping into an overhang it keeps going under it), never into rock below
c five mem Value=5
c gD greater
w ey.out gD.1
w five.out gD.2
c dn or TimeFrame=6
w gD.out dn.1
w in9 dn.2
c nwd not
w in0 nwd.in
c ud and
w dn.out ud.1
w nwd.out ud.2
c upv mem Value=-80
c dnv mem Value=80
c dm mux
w ud.out dm.set_input
w upv.out dm.signal_in0
w dnv.out dm.signal_in1
# after a detour: hold depth for 6 more seconds while moving across, so it passes the rock before homing again
c hold or TimeFrame=9
w bR.out hold.1
w bL.out hold.2
c km mem Value=-60
c hy mul ClampMin=-100 ClampMax=100
w vy.out hy.1
w km.out hy.2
c ym1 mux
w hold.out ym1.set_input
w cy.out ym1.signal_in0
w hy.out ym1.signal_in1
c ym mux
w blk.out ym.set_input
w ym1.out ym.signal_in0
w dm.out ym.signal_in1
# --- velocity_in, only while RETURN is on; 0,0 for 0.2 s when it's switched off
c cat concat Separator=,
w xm.out cat.1
w ym.out cat.2
c rel relay IsOn=false
w in6 rel.set_state
w cat.out rel.signal_in1
w rel.signal_out1 out1
c lvd delay Delay=0.2
c nlv not
c offE and
w in6 lvd.in nlv.in
w nlv.out offE.1
w lvd.out offE.2
c stop mem Value=0,0
c rel2 relay IsOn=false
w offE.out rel2.set_state
w stop.out rel2.signal_in1
w rel2.signal_out1 out1
# --- displays: distance and status
c ex2 mul
c ey2 mul
c ds add
c sq sqrt
c dr round
w ex.out ex2.1 ex2.2
w ey.out ey2.1 ey2.2
w ex2.out ds.1
w ey2.out ds.2
w ds.out sq.in
w sq.out dr.in ar.2
c um mem Value=m
c dcat concat Separator=" "
w dr.out dcat.1
w um.out dcat.2
w dcat.out out3
c three mem Value=3
c ar greater
w three.out ar.1
c sRet mem Value=RETURN
c sDet mem Value=DETOUR
c sArr mem Value=ARRIVED
c sMan mem Value=MANUAL
c m1 mux
c m2 mux
c m3 mux
w blk.out m1.set_input
w sRet.out m1.signal_in0
w sDet.out m1.signal_in1
w ar.out m2.set_input
w m1.out m2.signal_in0
w sArr.out m2.signal_in1
w in6 m3.set_input
w sMan.out m3.signal_in0
w m2.out m3.signal_in1
w m3.out out2
